Subject: [PATCH] lmi-camera: prerequisite plumbing for a second (front) camera source (R2)

R2 corrects two defects in R1:

  1. R1's argument parsing tested "argc == argi + 1" to mean "a duration was
     supplied", which inverted the test: it read strtol(argv[argc]) (a NULL
     pointer) when no duration was given and silently ignored the duration
     when one was. R2 uses "argc == argi + 2" (INPUT plus SECONDS) and bounds
     the argument count before any read.

  2. R1 added --camera-id to camera-test-capture.py but never passed
     --allow-non-rear-camera to the OEM diagnostic, so every non-zero camera
     id was still refused by the C policy gate. R2 threads one explicit
     authorization end to end: the Python layer refuses an unauthorized
     non-zero camera id before any runtime setup, forwards the authorization
     to the C binary, and the C gate honours it. The default remains
     rear-only in every layer.

R2 also widens the C argument bound from 5 to 6, so that an explicit camera
HAL path, a mode and the new authorization fit together, and prints the
HAL-reported facing so an operator can confirm the camera identity.

This patch remains a PREREQUISITE only. It adds no front camera, no UI
control, and it does not move the retractable camera mechanism. The
stepper/hall parameters for the pop-up live in the proprietary
vendor/etc/step_motor/mi_camera_config.xml and are not recoverable from any
public source or from the locally conserved materials; until they and the
OEM camera-id-to-module mapping are resolved, this patch must not be treated
as front-camera support. See implementation-plan.md.

Apply from the repository root with:  git apply --check fix.patch && git apply fix.patch
Revert with:                          git apply -R fix.patch
